{{!-- The featured post and the security feed, side by side.

     Why one partial that branches on the setting, instead of putting the grid in
     collection-layout.hbs: the hero must stay *exactly* where it is, full width, when
     no feed is configured — which is the default for every site that has not set
     `sec_feed_api_url`. A grid that is always present would reserve a 1/3 column for
     an absent widget and shrink the hero, and it would change the HTML of every
     collection page for no visible reason. So the grid exists only when the feed does.

     The duplicate `{{#match}}` below is the cost of that: a Handlebars partial cannot
     take an argument conditionally, and the alternative — always emitting the grid —
     costs every site a layout change it did not ask for. One line, one reason.

     `items-start` keeps the feed from stretching to the hero's height. `locale` only
     selects which hero partial renders; the feed gets its own strings from the page
     language. --}}
{{#if @custom.sec_feed_api_url}}
<div class="grid grid-cols-1 items-start gap-8 lg:grid-cols-3">
    {{!-- 2/3: the featured post. --}}
    <div class="lg:col-span-2">
        {{#match locale "=" "es"}}{{> "featured-hero-es"}}{{else match locale "=" "br"}}{{> "featured-hero-br"}}{{else}}{{> "featured-hero"}}{{/match}}
    </div>

    {{!-- 1/3: the security feed, as a column beside the hero. It carries no vertical
         margin of its own — the row owns the rhythm — and stacks below the hero on
         mobile, where the hero stays first. --}}
    <div class="lg:col-span-1">
        {{> "sec-feed" locale=locale}}
    </div>
</div>
{{else}}
{{#match locale "=" "es"}}{{> "featured-hero-es"}}{{else match locale "=" "br"}}{{> "featured-hero-br"}}{{else}}{{> "featured-hero"}}{{/match}}
{{/if}}